zed problems\"'!\n\n# Therefore: POT is solving a problem with effective reg = 0.1 * Cmax for raw cost\n# GeomLoss is solving with reg = 0.1 for raw cost\n# That'\"'s a huge difference\"'!\n\n# Let'\"'s compute: what reg for POT normalized gives the same as GeomLoss?\n# We need: POT_reg_norm * Cmax = GeomLoss_reg = 0.1\n# => POT_reg_norm = 0.1 / Cmax\n# But the canonical POT uses reg=0.1, which is way bigger than 0.1/Cmax\n\n# So the two Sinkhorn solves are for DIFFERENT regularization levels.\n# The POT one uses heavy regularization (small cost scale, relatively large reg)\n# The GeomLoss one uses light regularization (large cost scale, small reg)\n\n# This means we CAN'T unify them trivially.\n# But maybe we only need one? The batch-level transport just needs rough costs.\n# The potentials need finer detail.\n\nprint(f'\\\\\\\\nC_max = {C_max:.1f}')\nprint(f'POT effective reg (raw): {0.1 * C_max:.1f}')\nprint(f'GeomLoss reg (raw): 0.1')\n\\\" 2>&1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
